abstract: Fu ying xin shuo (婦嬰新說), written by Benjamin Hobson with Guan mao cai and catalogued as an 1858 Shanghai edition issued by Ren ji yi guan, discusses female reproductive anatomy, pregnancy, childbirth, childhood illness and historical remedies, with medical illustrations. This dataset draws on Bodleian Libraries, University of Oxford, Sinica 1792. It provides a source-faithful transcription of 128 faces and a bibliographical and circulation-history guide for the nine faces p129–137, without reproducing that chapter’s operational text. JSON, TXT and TEI preserve source characters, printed punctuation, small notes and diagram labels, with links to the witness, for preliminary research in medical history, translation and illustration. Version 0.1.0 is an AI image transcription with same-witness supplementation; independent collation has not been applied. Twelve bounded uncertainty records remain, and no human full-text collation is claimed.
